SUMMARY:Bat Week Screening of “The Invisible Mammal” and Davis Premiere
DESCRIPTION:Join cast\, crew and our screening partners on Thursday\, October 15\, 2026 for a special Bat Week event: the Davis\, CA Premiere of The Invisible Mammal\, the award-winning feature documentary about bat conservation.\nAgainst the backdrop of the sixth mass extinction\, an all-woman team of biologists set out to save bats from a deadly fungal disease. But when the COVID-19 pandemic interrupts their work\, they are sent down a path of discovery that illuminates the connections between bat conservation and preventing the spread of infectious disease. \nMeet director Kristin Tièche and castmember Corky Quirk and her ambassador bats! \nCOME IN COSTUME! It’s Bat Week after all! Bat and vampire attire are encouraged! \n  \nSchedule:\n6:00 pm – Doors open \n6:30 pm – Screening begins \n8:00 pm – Q&A with cast and crew \n8:30 pm – Tabling in lobby \n  \nTicketing:\nPlease purchase tickets in advance\, and take advantage of our early bird pricing: \nNow to Oct 15\, 2026: $15 + fees \nOct 16-30\, 2026: $18 + fees
URL:https://visitdavis.org/event/bat-week-screening-of-the-invisible-mammal-and-davis-premiere/
LOCATION:Davis Veterans Memorial Theater\, 277 E. 14th Street\, Davis CA\, Davis\, 95616\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitdavis.org/wp-content/uploads/The-Invisible-Mammal-Davis-Flyer-scaled-3kLtcv.jpg
END:VEVENT
